            {
              "message": "The first-run test executes an extracted shell fragment with no-op `git` and `cargo` shims, then checks two independent logs. It therefore passes if `cargo generate-lockfile` moves after the initial commit or `bootstrap` moves before it, and it never verifies the required HEAD, committed Cargo.lock, or hooks state. AC-01/CN-02 remain insufficiently covered; exercise the public task and assert a single cross-command order and resulting state.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "apps/cli/tests/consumer_scaffold_host_first.rs",
              "line": 250,
              "category": "test_coverage"
            },
            {
              "message": "The exported task-set assertion proves that the scaffold contains `init`, but nothing asserts that the source repository's root Makefile does not contain it. Adding `[tasks.init]` to the maintainer Makefile would violate AC-03 while this suite still passes.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "apps/cli/tests/consumer_scaffold_host_first.rs",
              "line": 170,
              "category": "test_coverage"
            },
            {
              "message": "The AC-05 check uses independent substring assertions rather than validating the fallback instruction. In `adr2pr.md`, `contains(\"text\")` is already satisfied by the unrelated word `context`, and a contradictory phrase such as `do not continue` still satisfies `contains(\"continue\")`. A regression removing or reversing the text-progress fallback can therefore pass.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "apps/cli/tests/consumer_scaffold_host_first.rs",
              "line": 301,
