        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The missing-identity assertion cannot pass against the current exported task: the task logs `git ... init -b main` before the `git var` probes, while this assertion rejects any trace containing an `init` argument. Cleanup removes `.git` but does not remove that trace entry. The success-path `expected_sequence` at lines 380–383 also explicitly codifies the conflicting init-before-probes order. Align the expected sequence and implementation contract so identity probing occurs before `git init`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "apps/cli/tests/consumer_scaffold_host_first.rs",
              "line": 351,
              "category": "testing"
            },
            {
              "message": "The catchup workflow regression check uses independent whole-file `contains` calls for the repository condition and its command. It therefore passes when those phrases occur in unrelated sections or when the command appears in a negated instruction—the exact false-positive shape prohibited by the briefing. Assert the complete instruction or an adjacent-line/structured association between each condition and command.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "apps/cli/tests/consumer_scaffold_host_first.rs",
              "line": 493,
              "category": "testing"
            }
