        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The identity-failure trace check does not actually forbid the commit command: it searches for `git commit`, but the tested command is emitted as `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit`, so that substring cannot match. A regression that commits before failing could pass this assertion. Check the actual command form (or assert no trace line whose final operation is `commit`).",
