        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The precheck only reads `user.name`/`user.email` from global config and ignores Git's other config scopes and supported email fallback. A valid identity can therefore be rejected even though `git commit` would succeed. Use Git's actual identity resolution for the check.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "overlay/Makefile.toml",
              "line": 33,
              "category": "incorrect-identity-resolution"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:db48260db51e83a1bcde08dda04de097ebdb7ac12d6a2bbafd436f60d0f02360",
          "at": "2026-07-25T00:06:30Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "zero_findings",
          "findings": [],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:763b95f39705819521d0695449646b25add692173fce984a95c97872187837fd",
          "at": "2026-07-25T00:10:38Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "This preflight runs before the target has a `.git` directory, so Git cannot activate identity settings from global `includeIf \"gitdir:...\"` or `includeIf \"onbranch:...\"` blocks. After `git init -b main`, the actual commit would activate those blocks and could succeed, while the preflight incorrectly rejects the same setup. Validate identity in the initialized repository under rollback protection, before generating the lockfile, or otherwise account for conditional includes.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "overlay/Makefile.toml",
              "line": 34,
              "category": "incorrect-identity-resolution"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:763b95f39705819521d0695449646b25add692173fce984a95c97872187837fd",
          "at": "2026-07-25T00:25:43Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The identity check now runs after `git init`, so the prerequisite check itself performs a filesystem side effect and briefly creates `.git` before rejecting an invalid identity. This violates the stated requirement that identity validation precede side-effecting initialization. Move the `git var` checks before `git init`; retain the rollback trap for later failures.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "overlay/Makefile.toml",
              "line": 52,
              "category": "precondition-ordering"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:9daa1614c59f01c317726e2f2bad7e300a01c253bc017433b8484e712180156e",
          "at": "2026-07-25T00:53:16Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "These `git var` calls run before the target repository exists, so they do not use the same configuration context as the later commit. When the scaffold is inside another repository, Git can read identity from the parent `.git/config` and pass this check; after `git init`, the fresh nested repository hides that config and `git commit` still fails and rolls everything back. Conversely, identity supplied through a conditional include matching the new repository is unavailable during this check. Validate in the initialized target repository under rollback protection, before lockfile generation, so failure still leaves no artifacts.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "overlay/Makefile.toml",
              "line": 33,
              "category": "incorrect-identity-resolution"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:f41daf79544b54fde19607cc72b78435da43735e6f6634cfc9619548acdefe8e",
          "at": "2026-07-25T00:56:13Z"
